---
import disagreementData from "../../../../public/data/surf-forecast/disagreement.json";
import { ft } from "../../../lib/surf-forecast/findings";

const lead = disagreementData.rows.find((r) => r.lead_days === 3);
if (!lead) throw new Error("no lead-3 disagreement row");
const low = lead.bins[0];
const high = lead.bins[lead.bins.length - 1];
const ratio = (high.mae / low.mae).toFixed(1);
// Is the bottom of the range flat? Compare the lowest two fifths.
const bottomFlat = Math.abs(lead.bins[1].mae - lead.bins[0].mae) / lead.bins[0].mae < 0.05;
const averagingWorse = lead.consensus_mae > lead.ecmwf_mae;
// The caption claims the other leads share the shape; check it rather than assert it.
const sameShapeElsewhere = disagreementData.rows
	.filter((r) => r.lead_days !== 3)
	.every((r) => r.bins[r.bins.length - 1].mae > 1.2 * r.bins[0].mae);
---

<section id="disagreement" class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 md:px-12 md:py-20">
	<h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-3xl">When the forecasts disagree, trust them less</h2>
	<div class="mt-3 max-w-[65ch] space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
		<p>
			Check three forecasts and they rarely agree. At the buoys, where the answer is known, that disagreement can be
			tested: rank each buoy's days by how far apart the three systems were, and see whether the best one does worse on
			the days they argued. It does. On a buoy's lowest-disagreement days ECMWF misses by {ft(low.mae)} ft three days
			out; on its highest, by {ft(high.mae)} ft, {ratio} times as much.
			{bottomFlat && <> The lowest two fifths are flat: the warning only switches on when the disagreement is unusual for that spot.</>}
		</p>
		<p>
			The ranking is done within each buoy on purpose. A sheltered buoy has permanently high disagreement and
			permanently high error for the same reason, and pooling every buoy together would make disagreement look
			predictive even if, at any single spot, it told you nothing.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div id="fg-disagreement" class="mt-8">
		<div class="flex justify-end">
			<button type="button" data-vg-table-toggle class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-accent-blue" aria-pressed="false">
				View as table
			</button>
		</div>
		<div data-vg-chart class="mt-2 overflow-x-auto"></div>
		<div data-vg-table class="mt-2 overflow-x-auto"></div>
		<p class="mt-3 font-mono text-[0.7rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
			Wave height, three days out. Disagreement is the range of the ECMWF, NOAA and DWD forecasts for the same hour,
			ranked within each buoy.{sameShapeElsewhere && " One and five days out show the same shape; see the table."}
		</p>
	</div>

	{
		averagingWorse && (
			<p class="mt-8 max-w-[65ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
				One tempting fix does not work: averaging the three. Three days out the plain average misses by
				{" "}{ft(lead.consensus_mae)} ft against {ft(lead.ecmwf_mae)} ft for ECMWF alone, because DWD's large bias drags
				the average with it. Averaging forecasts only helps when their errors are independent and unbiased, and these
				are neither.
			</p>
		)
	}

	<script src="../../../scripts/surf-forecast/disagreement-chart.ts"></script>
</section>
